Subject: [PATCH] musl: Give the malloc_trim fallback a private name

The musl-bsd malloc.h overlay declares an external malloc_trim. Defining
systemd's static fallback with the same name after include_next conflicts
with that declaration.

Keep the no-op fallback under a private name and redirect callers to it,
as the other musl wrappers do. This also works without the overlay and
does not introduce a link dependency on libmusl-bsd.

diff --git a/src/include/musl/malloc.h b/src/include/musl/malloc.h
--- a/src/include/musl/malloc.h
+++ b/src/include/musl/malloc.h
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
         return -1;
 }

-static inline int malloc_trim(size_t pad) {
+static inline int missing_malloc_trim(size_t pad) {
         return 0;
 }
+#define malloc_trim missing_malloc_trim
